  "summary": "src/main.ts builds the forest scene and passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or looked at it in a browser. It has a ground plane and three instanced meshes from a fixed seed (12345): 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (spheres). That makes 8,000 trees and 2,000 rocks, with the trunk and canopy each instanced. Canopies get per-instance green hsl colours and rocks get per-instance grey hsl colours. There is a hemisphere light and one shadow-casting directional light. Fog is `effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"`. The orbit camera auto-rotates slowly (`autoRotate: 0.12`) around the whole forest. After `app.ready()` it sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` two animation frames later, so the first frame should already be drawn. I didn't write a separate `requestAnimationFrame` loop because `createAuraApp` runs the render loop.",
